<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia's Cadenalco Q1 net up 20 pct.</title>
<headline>Colombia's Cadenalco Q1 net up 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cadenalco, Colombia's largest retailer in terms of overall sales and size, said its first-quarter net profit rose to 3.8 billion pesos from 3.1 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>The 20 percent gain in profitability was coupled with a 17.1 percent increase in operating income, Cadenalco said, adding that its total assets had risen 34 percent to more than 123 billion pesos.</p>
<p>Cadenalco operates in five different retail formats and its holdings include two supermarket chains and two general merchandise chains.</p>
<p>((-- Tom Brown, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
